zeron (https://github.com/zeronsh/zeron)

Some interface behaviour in AOZUMI Agents is a close translation of zeron's
desktop client at commit 911ec56, re-implemented in React from a written
description (docs/aozumi/ZERON-UI-SPEC.md). No zeron source code, brand, logo,
loaders, colors or sounds are used. The translated pieces and their constants
are:
- Stick-to-bottom scrolling: user-only detach, 2 px / 70 px re-engage, the
  jump pill's 320 px hysteresis, and the follow spring
  (gui/apps/app/src/components/ui/stick-to-bottom.ts).
- Streaming Markdown by blocks: the second-to-last-block boundary, the
  lazy-continuation step back, full reparse with link reference
  definitions, and the display-only mending rules for the last block
  (gui/apps/app/src/components/thread/timeline/streaming-markdown-blocks.ts).
- The streaming text veil: per-chunk tracking on the common prefix, the
  adaptive duration (EMA seeded at 160 ms, 0.7/0.3, gaps capped at
  1000 ms, 3 x EMA clamped to 120-400 ms, faster past two chunks) and the
  1.6-power opacity curve
  (gui/apps/app/src/components/thread/timeline/veil.ts and rehype-veil.ts).
- The own-send runway: park the new prompt near the top, reserve the space
  below it, glide keeping 85% of the remaining distance per frame, and hand
  back to the pin once the reply fills the reservation
  (gui/apps/app/src/components/ui/send-runway.ts).
- Tool-group folding (a user pin over auto-open, auto-open while live) and
  the arrival stagger (first row after 90 ms, then 65 ms apart, rows
  present on open never animate)
  (gui/apps/app/src/components/thread/timeline/activity-group.ts).
- The working trailer's rotation rule (seeded per session, a new word every
  7 s) and its elapsed-time format. The word list, the dot loader and its
  colours are AOZUMI's own
  (gui/apps/app/src/components/thread/timeline/working-trailer.ts).
- The composer's text box cap (260 px) and its 180 ms ease-out height morph
  with the bottom edge held still
  (gui/apps/app/src/components/promptbox/composer-height-morph.ts).

